1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:01,976
(Previously)
If you don't want to borrow my money,

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,176
how about you let me invest in your company?

3
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:05,760
No one has ever believed in me
this much in my entire life.

4
00:00:05,880 --> 00:00:08,560
I don't even know what I'll be like
when I get out of the military.

5
00:00:08,920 --> 00:00:10,200
When my friend moves to Dubai,

6
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:11,880
I'll definitely miss him.

7
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:14,960
Next time, please tell me things right away.

8
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:16,536
Don't let me find out from someone else.

9
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:17,760
But I'm so happy for you.

10
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:19,360
You made your dream come true.

11
00:00:19,440 --> 00:00:20,600
The foundation just called.

12
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:21,720
A plane crashed.

13
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:22,520
Hey!
Please check on Kanit.

14
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:24,200
- His leg is badly hurt.
- Are you okay?

15
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:25,480
Just the thought of losing you

16
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:26,680
is more than I can bear.

17
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:34,640
Ouch!

18
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:36,200
Hey!

19
00:00:36,360 --> 00:00:37,360
What's wrong?

20
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:39,936
Why didn't you tell me what you wanted?

21
00:00:39,960 --> 00:00:40,960
Come here.

22
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:43,040
Be gentle.

23
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:47,600
What do you want?

24
00:00:47,640 --> 00:00:48,640
My phone.

25
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:50,800
Here.

26
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:53,240
The rice porridge is ready.

27
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:54,400
I made you an omelet too.

28
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:56,680
It looks so good.

29
00:00:56,840 --> 00:00:57,840
Come on.

30
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:03,040
Food is served. Enjoy.

31
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:06,896
What did the doctor say yesterday?
When can you get your cast off?

32
00:01:06,920 --> 00:01:08,880
In about two weeks.

33
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:10,680
Is it itchy?

34
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:12,120
A little.

35
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:16,160
I'll scratch it for you.

36
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:19,720
Hey.
Go deeper.

37
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:21,440
A little deeper.

38
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:22,560
Yes, right there.

39
00:01:23,360 --> 00:01:24,600
Ah, so good.

40
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:25,800
Right there.

41
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:26,720
Ah.

42
00:01:26,880 --> 00:01:28,000
A little harder.

43
00:01:28,080 --> 00:01:29,240
Ah.

44
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:31,600
If you're itchy somewhere else,
I can help with that too.

45
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:32,760
For free.

46
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:34,520
You pervert.

47
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:37,000
My leg hurts. Who would be in the mood?

48
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:38,040
Well…

49
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:39,600
Just in case you are.

50
00:01:40,480 --> 00:01:41,280
Are you really not in the mood?

51
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:42,320
No.

52
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:44,800
Is it still itchy?

53
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:45,880
Not anymore.

54
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:49,880
Hey, while your leg is like this,

55
00:01:50,280 --> 00:01:51,440
you need to keep it elevated

56
00:01:51,520 --> 00:01:52,680
so it doesn't swell.

57
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:53,560
Ouch!

58
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:54,600
It feels tight.

59
00:01:56,480 --> 00:01:57,600
Just sit like this.

60
00:01:58,360 --> 00:02:00,200
Once you're done eating, take your medicine.

61
00:02:00,720 --> 00:02:01,856
This one's for after your meal.

62
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:03,800
This helps with the pain.
This reduces swelling.

63
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:07,400
You remember everything so well,
even though you're not the one taking them.

64
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:10,080
That's because I pay attention.

65
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:15,040
Ow! That hurts!

66
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:19,880
I'm taking you
to get your dressing changed this afternoon.

67
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:21,800
Does it smell yet?

68
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:23,520
Gross.

69
00:02:23,840 --> 00:02:24,800
You're a flight attendant with a broken wing.

70
00:02:24,840 --> 00:02:26,120
I have to take good care of you.

71
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:27,680
Come on.

72
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:30,120
Eat it while it's still hot.

73
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:34,560
This smells so good. Come on.

74
00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:39,280
It's skinless chicken.

75
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:41,280
Blow on it for me.

76
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:47,000
I'm just testing it for you.

77
00:02:47,040 --> 00:02:48,440
Ugh, gross.

78
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:49,480
Come on.

79
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:06,280
What are you looking at?

80
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:13,560
What?
In two days?

81
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:15,560
Mm.

82
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:18,120
But look at me.

83
00:03:18,880 --> 00:03:20,000
I don't think I can make it.

84
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:21,480
Why don't you call them?

85
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:23,720
Just tell them you have an emergency.

86
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:24,960
Ask if you can postpone it.

87
00:03:25,040 --> 00:03:26,200
You can join the next round.

88
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:28,200
I can't do that.

89
00:03:28,200 --> 00:03:29,320
No one does that.

90
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:31,600
The next round probably won't be
until next year.

91
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:35,000
Then I'm taking you.

92
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:36,120
To where?
To talk to the airline.

93
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:39,160
Come on.
Let's go now.

94
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:40,440
Hey.
Slowly.
Hold on.

95
00:03:41,440 --> 00:03:42,600
Are you sure you're okay?

96
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:44,320
Don't push yourself. You'll hurt your back.

97
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:48,280
It's your dream.

98
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:52,160
If I can't be a flight attendant,
there are other things I can do.

99
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:58,000
I'm so lucky to have even survived
that accident.

100
00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:02,880
I have no dreams left
other than spending time with you.

101
00:05:16,500 --> 00:05:18,500
"A Dog and A Plane"
(Episode 10)

102
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:26,000
Here.

103
00:05:27,840 --> 00:05:29,920
Damn, I feel so bad for you.

104
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,480
You only just started teaching here.

105
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:32,560
Yeah.

106
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:33,840
I was having fun.

107
00:05:34,280 --> 00:05:35,720
I thought I could make it long-term.

108
00:05:36,200 --> 00:05:37,240
Seriously, man.

109
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:39,256
Things were just starting
to get back on track for you.

110
00:05:39,280 --> 00:05:41,000
But you should be fine.
It's only two years.

111
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:42,760
You can come back and apply again.

112
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:44,480
Two whole years.

113
00:05:45,080 --> 00:05:47,200
Who knows what opportunities I'll miss,

114
00:05:47,640 --> 00:05:49,280
instead of getting to do what I love?

115
00:05:50,080 --> 00:05:51,080
It's okay.

116
00:05:51,320 --> 00:05:52,400
You can always come back.

117
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:54,800
Yeah.

118
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:11,160
Bye.

119
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:12,600
Get home safe.

120
00:06:15,880 --> 00:06:16,880
Bye.

121
00:06:17,160 --> 00:06:18,280
Get home safe.

122
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:25,120
VEHA

123
00:06:34,040 --> 00:06:35,040
Bye.

124
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:44,680
WHY WON'T YOU PICK UP THE PHONE?

125
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:48,720
I'M TEACHING.

126
00:06:51,440 --> 00:06:53,560
STANDING AT THE GATE DOESN'T
REALLY COUNT AS TEACHING.

127
00:06:57,400 --> 00:06:58,680
- Bye.
- Bye.

128
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:24,120
Come on!

129
00:07:24,160 --> 00:07:25,160
Focus!

130
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:26,800
Move over!

131
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:29,200
Faster!

132
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:31,800
Come on!

133
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:35,280
You won't pick up the phone
or reply to my texts.

134
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:37,000
Why are you avoiding me?

135
00:07:38,440 --> 00:07:39,640
I've been busy.

136
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:42,760
Handling my resignation,
handing over my classes.

137
00:07:43,320 --> 00:07:45,560
Not to mention,
preparing my paperwork for the military.

138
00:07:45,760 --> 00:07:46,880
Stop with your excuses.

139
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:49,240
It's just picking up the phone.
Is it that hard?

140
00:07:50,120 --> 00:07:52,640
You're not even looking at me
when I'm talking to you right now.

141
00:07:54,160 --> 00:07:55,160
Look at me.

142
00:07:55,680 --> 00:07:56,960
Say what's on your mind.

143
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:05,200
I'll be away for two years.

144
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,400
I don't want you to wait for me.

145
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:10,600
Why did you say that?

146
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:13,000
We've talked about this.

147
00:08:13,440 --> 00:08:16,040
You'll hang in there, and I'll wait.

148
00:08:17,360 --> 00:08:19,240
I don't want a promise to tie us down.

149
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:21,360
It's a whole two years.

150
00:08:21,600 --> 00:08:24,880
If you find someone better than me,
you deserve it.

151
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:27,720
You deserve to find someone
with a better future.

152
00:08:29,280 --> 00:08:30,960
Why are you assuming things on your own?

153
00:08:31,720 --> 00:08:33,960
These are my feelings. I'll deal with them.

154
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:36,160
These are my feelings too.

155
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:38,760
I don't want you to worry.

156
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:41,240
I don't know what's going to happen to me.

157
00:08:41,400 --> 00:08:43,000
What's going to happen to you?

158
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:44,800
You'll be fine.

159
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:46,600
I'll visit you.

160
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:48,200
And then you'll get out of there.

161
00:08:48,760 --> 00:08:51,840
Telling me to find someone else
is so insulting.

162
00:08:52,720 --> 00:08:55,400
Do you know how many years I waited
for you before we got together?

163
00:08:56,560 --> 00:08:59,440
What makes you think
I can't wait another two damn years?

164
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:04,680
What's wrong with you?

165
00:09:32,880 --> 00:09:33,880
Hello.

166
00:09:34,280 --> 00:09:36,960
(Hello. I'm calling from Magic Sky Airway.)

167
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:39,040
Oh, hello.

168
00:09:39,560 --> 00:09:43,000
(We'd like you to come in
for reporting and training.)

169
00:09:43,160 --> 00:09:44,720
(The management was impressed)

170
00:09:44,720 --> 00:09:47,600
(by how you helped the passengers
during the accident the other day.)

171
00:09:48,640 --> 00:09:49,640
Really?

172
00:09:50,240 --> 00:09:51,240
Thank you.

173
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:54,440
(You're welcome.
We'll send you the details by email.)

174
00:09:55,200 --> 00:09:56,720
Sure. Thank you so much.

175
00:10:00,160 --> 00:10:01,160
To!

176
00:10:01,560 --> 00:10:02,080
To!

177
00:10:02,080 --> 00:10:03,120
Hey! What's wrong?

178
00:10:04,400 --> 00:10:05,400
Hey.

179
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:07,640
Magic Sky Airway called me in to start.

180
00:10:08,040 --> 00:10:09,040
Oh!

181
00:10:09,320 --> 00:10:10,560
I'm happy for you!

182
00:10:19,520 --> 00:10:20,520
Hey.

183
00:10:21,280 --> 00:10:22,560
Are you really happy?

184
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:23,960
Yes.

185
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:25,280
Are you okay?

186
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:30,960
I'm happy for you.

187
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:33,760
But I'm worried about you.

188
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:36,640
You just got into an accident.

189
00:10:37,080 --> 00:10:39,280
I don't want you to go through
anything like that again.

190
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:44,280
You know that accidents can't be predicted.

191
00:10:45,040 --> 00:10:46,640
You should know that better than anyone.

192
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:51,000
I understand.

193
00:10:52,920 --> 00:10:54,200
It's your dream.

194
00:10:55,160 --> 00:10:56,400
I'm willing to support you.

195
00:10:59,120 --> 00:11:02,280
But I'm going to be based overseas.

196
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:12,160
What about our business?

197
00:11:14,120 --> 00:11:15,520
Don't worry about that.

198
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:17,000
I'll take care of it.

199
00:11:17,520 --> 00:11:19,080
That's my dream too.

200
00:11:20,960 --> 00:11:23,160
Let's each chase our own dreams,

201
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:25,720
then meet back in the middle for ours.

202
00:11:26,480 --> 00:11:27,480
Is that okay?

203
00:11:30,520 --> 00:11:33,120
I'm so lucky to have a boyfriend
who understands me.

204
00:11:35,160 --> 00:11:36,400
I'm so damn proud of you.

205
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:42,040
Hey!

206
00:11:46,840 --> 00:11:48,000
What are you doing?

207
00:11:48,320 --> 00:11:49,920
I guess we have to shower together now.

208
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:32,160
What are you working on?

209
00:12:32,880 --> 00:12:34,440
A will leaving all your assets to me?

210
00:12:34,560 --> 00:12:35,560
Whoa.

211
00:12:36,560 --> 00:12:38,240
Wishing me dead already?

212
00:12:39,080 --> 00:12:39,920
Come on.

213
00:12:40,040 --> 00:12:42,640
Breaking down all this money?
What else could it be?

214
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:44,200
Saving up money to get married?

215
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:47,800
Look.

216
00:12:47,840 --> 00:12:49,840
How could I marry anyone
with just this much money?

217
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:53,440
Oh, bro.

218
00:12:53,560 --> 00:12:55,080
Why is love so expensive?

219
00:12:55,480 --> 00:12:58,280
Can't you just show your sincerity
and make a promise?

220
00:12:59,120 --> 00:13:00,800
Being romantic doesn't pay the bills.

221
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:03,080
You need money in your bank account
to prove it.

222
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:08,280
Love has no place for poor people, huh?

223
00:13:10,360 --> 00:13:11,800
I'll work hard when I grow up.

224
00:13:36,280 --> 00:13:37,480
- Je, hi.
- Oh.

225
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:40,000
It's the wrong time to be craving
minced meat salad.

226
00:13:41,640 --> 00:13:42,720
I'm here to talk business.

227
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:44,560
Scammer!

228
00:13:44,800 --> 00:13:46,800
- Serving politicians!
- No!

229
00:13:46,800 --> 00:13:48,480
If it's shady, I'm out.

230
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:49,400
Don't even ask me.
It's nothing like that.

231
00:13:50,320 --> 00:13:51,616
You're already rich. I don't even need to ask.

232
00:13:51,640 --> 00:13:53,336
I want to rent the second floor for my office.

233
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:54,360
No way.

234
00:13:54,480 --> 00:13:55,000
What?
Isn't that too fast?

235
00:13:55,800 --> 00:13:56,800
No way.

236
00:13:57,040 --> 00:13:57,720
Je!
We can discuss the rent.

237
00:13:58,640 --> 00:13:59,680
No way!

238
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:00,840
Je!

239
00:14:00,880 --> 00:14:02,080
I'm giving it to you for free.

240
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:07,080
I don't want to run a minced meat salad business.

241
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:09,456
Oh, I'm definitely not
letting you take over my business.

242
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:11,000
If I gave you my recipe,

243
00:14:11,040 --> 00:14:13,440
you'd only ruin it.

244
00:14:14,560 --> 00:14:16,200
Now that I think about it,

245
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:18,960
what happened that day

246
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:21,600
made me realize

247
00:14:22,680 --> 00:14:24,880
life is so short.

248
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:28,200
You never know if you'll die tomorrow.

249
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:31,600
Who am I talking to?

250
00:14:31,760 --> 00:14:33,000
- I'm here.
- Yeah.

251
00:14:33,640 --> 00:14:35,560
I've saved money my whole life.

252
00:14:35,760 --> 00:14:37,800
Who knows if I'll ever get to spend it?

253
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:39,600
So I've decided.

254
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:41,880
I'm going to travel.

255
00:14:42,280 --> 00:14:44,440
I'm going to spend all my money
traveling the world.

256
00:14:44,680 --> 00:14:48,280
See the wonders of the Ancient World,
the Middle Ages, and the New World.

257
00:14:48,320 --> 00:14:49,320
I'll see it all.

258
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:52,680
I'm sure there must be another Stonehenge
and another pyramid somewhere else.

259
00:14:54,520 --> 00:14:56,080
Must be nice to be rich.

260
00:14:56,120 --> 00:14:57,480
You get to do everything you want.

261
00:14:58,600 --> 00:14:59,760
Don't be jealous of me.

262
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:02,400
This building is yours.

263
00:15:03,160 --> 00:15:04,000
But…
give me my shares.

264
00:15:04,920 --> 00:15:05,680
Who knows?

265
00:15:05,720 --> 00:15:09,040
If your business hits it big
and becomes a unicorn like Komsan Lee's,

266
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:11,440
I'm going to sell my shares

267
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:14,280
and use the money to explore
the wonders outside the world.

268
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:16,960
So let me learn an alien language now.

269
00:15:23,080 --> 00:15:24,480
Je! Be serious!

270
00:15:25,080 --> 00:15:27,160
Do you see the potential
or just sympathize with me?

271
00:15:27,200 --> 00:15:28,240
I sympathize with you.

272
00:15:29,040 --> 00:15:30,040
Seriously?

273
00:15:30,720 --> 00:15:32,000
Look, To.

274
00:15:32,120 --> 00:15:34,480
I see your effort.

275
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:38,760
If I don't see the value
and help someone who's trying,

276
00:15:38,960 --> 00:15:42,160
who the hell do you expect me to help?

277
00:15:44,960 --> 00:15:48,360
So I'll be able to save up faster
for my marriage.

278
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:52,360
When you're a CEO,
everyone wants you to be their son-in-law.

279
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:53,840
Thank you, Je.

280
00:15:54,880 --> 00:15:55,880
Can I get a hug?

281
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:56,680
What?

282
00:15:56,720 --> 00:15:57,720
No!

283
00:15:58,040 --> 00:15:59,320
You're so kind!

284
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:01,520
It kinda feels like I'm your dad and mom.

285
00:16:01,880 --> 00:16:02,880
You're both.

286
00:16:12,160 --> 00:16:13,160
Je!

287
00:16:27,240 --> 00:16:28,240
Hey, Ki.

288
00:16:28,480 --> 00:16:30,480
Aren't you taking shifts
at the foundation anymore?

289
00:16:30,600 --> 00:16:31,600
Are you busy?

290
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:36,000
I just don't want him to find me there.

291
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:38,000
Who?

292
00:16:38,120 --> 00:16:39,120
Veha?

293
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:42,960
I'm going into the army in just a few days.

294
00:16:43,280 --> 00:16:44,400
I don't want to see him.

295
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:46,880
I'm scared I'll cave
and try to make up with him.

296
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:48,600
Please. You're scared of caving?

297
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:50,480
What you're doing to him

298
00:16:50,680 --> 00:16:51,840
is so mean, you know?

299
00:16:55,480 --> 00:16:57,160
You don't need to rub it in.

300
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:07,360
Did you eat all my gummies?

301
00:17:07,440 --> 00:17:08,440
Yeah.

302
00:17:08,560 --> 00:17:09,560
It's good.

303
00:17:10,560 --> 00:17:11,680
I'll grab more.

304
00:17:11,840 --> 00:17:14,400
Wow, you're complaining?

305
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:18,040
Alright.

306
00:17:19,280 --> 00:17:20,600
I won't rub salt in the wound.

307
00:17:20,720 --> 00:17:24,000
But I'm going to say something,
and it's not that I'm trying to lecture you.

308
00:17:25,080 --> 00:17:27,680
Soon, you won't get to see him anymore.

309
00:17:28,280 --> 00:17:30,920
So I think you should
use the time you have left

310
00:17:31,720 --> 00:17:32,880
to see him.

311
00:17:34,080 --> 00:17:37,280
Stop with your romantic act.

312
00:17:37,720 --> 00:17:38,720
That's so outdated.

313
00:17:39,080 --> 00:17:40,560
Love is a sacrifice?

314
00:17:41,720 --> 00:17:43,160
That's ancient, Ki.

315
00:17:43,560 --> 00:17:46,360
If you really love him, you have to be selfish.

316
00:17:46,600 --> 00:17:48,440
You shouldn't let him find someone better,

317
00:17:48,920 --> 00:17:50,840
because you're the best.

318
00:17:55,280 --> 00:17:56,600
You think I should see him?

319
00:17:57,240 --> 00:17:59,400
At least, if he comes to see you,

320
00:17:59,920 --> 00:18:01,080
just don't run away.

321
00:18:04,480 --> 00:18:05,480
Mm.

322
00:18:05,840 --> 00:18:06,840
Okay.

323
00:18:07,560 --> 00:18:09,040
Mm. Good.

324
00:18:09,800 --> 00:18:10,800
There he is.

325
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:27,520
How did you get here?

326
00:18:28,080 --> 00:18:29,720
I saw Beer when I went to the foundation.

327
00:18:30,120 --> 00:18:31,440
He told me to come find you here.

328
00:18:37,520 --> 00:18:39,080
Why did you cut your hair like that?

329
00:18:39,680 --> 00:18:40,600
Why are you doing this?

330
00:18:40,600 --> 00:18:43,000
I want to show you that I'm sincere.

331
00:18:43,400 --> 00:18:45,360
I even prepared a military application.

332
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:47,760
So neither of us has to wait for each other.

333
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:49,000
I'm going in with you.

334
00:18:49,040 --> 00:18:50,040
Are you crazy?

335
00:18:50,080 --> 00:18:52,000
You can't leave your good life for me.

336
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:53,680
My good life

337
00:18:53,760 --> 00:18:55,000
means having you in it.

338
00:18:55,760 --> 00:18:57,160
I won't give up.

339
00:18:58,320 --> 00:19:00,000
I won't let you leave me.

340
00:19:01,960 --> 00:19:05,120
I waited for so long before we got together.

341
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:09,800
Nothing can stop us now.

342
00:19:10,680 --> 00:19:13,240
Except you,
who's scared of god knows what.

343
00:19:16,280 --> 00:19:17,720
I never want to leave you, Veha.

344
00:19:19,600 --> 00:19:21,440
I just want you to find someone better.

345
00:19:21,880 --> 00:19:23,680
There's no one better.

346
00:19:24,960 --> 00:19:26,640
My heart is with you.

347
00:19:28,920 --> 00:19:30,480
What can I do to make you believe me?

348
00:19:30,600 --> 00:19:32,280
Squat jump 100 times?

349
00:19:33,280 --> 00:19:34,480
Hey!

350
00:19:36,440 --> 00:19:37,440
No.

351
00:19:39,840 --> 00:19:40,840
I'm sorry.

352
00:19:41,560 --> 00:19:43,240
I'm sorry for underestimating your heart.

353
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:47,840
Don't ever say you'll leave me again.

354
00:19:53,720 --> 00:19:56,480
This haircut looks hot on you.

355
00:19:57,400 --> 00:19:59,400
Pretty sexy. I like it.

356
00:20:03,920 --> 00:20:06,480
Sexy? It's so dorky.

357
00:20:07,840 --> 00:20:11,240
But if it could make you believe
that I'll wait for you, I'm okay with it.

358
00:20:15,320 --> 00:20:16,160
Okay.

359
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:17,480
I believe you now.

360
00:20:38,720 --> 00:20:40,040
Please fasten your seatbelts.

361
00:20:41,480 --> 00:20:42,480
Sir,

362
00:20:42,760 --> 00:20:45,160
please adjust your seat
to the upright position.

363
00:20:45,400 --> 00:20:46,400
Thank you.

364
00:20:48,400 --> 00:20:49,400
Thank you.

365
00:20:54,040 --> 00:20:54,840
What?

366
00:20:54,880 --> 00:20:55,880
What's going on?

367
00:21:01,720 --> 00:21:03,000
May I help you with anything?

368
00:21:19,960 --> 00:21:20,960
Oh.

369
00:21:22,360 --> 00:21:23,360
What are you doing here?

370
00:21:23,760 --> 00:21:25,280
I'm here to make your dream come true.

371
00:21:30,120 --> 00:21:31,120
Hey.

372
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:34,320
You're making a scene.
Aren't you disturbing the other passengers?

373
00:21:34,800 --> 00:21:36,200
I already told everyone.

374
00:21:36,880 --> 00:21:38,720
They're willing to be my witness.

375
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:39,720
Right?

376
00:21:39,720 --> 00:21:41,160
Yes.

377
00:21:44,080 --> 00:21:45,520
Alright.

378
00:21:46,120 --> 00:21:47,680
What did you prepare to surprise me?

379
00:21:49,440 --> 00:21:50,440
No surprise.

380
00:21:52,600 --> 00:21:55,160
I'm just a handsome, rugged guy
who loves you as much as the sky.

381
00:21:56,080 --> 00:21:58,120
Ready to get down on one knee
and tell my boyfriend.

382
00:22:01,520 --> 00:22:03,680
I'm ready to take care of him
for the rest of his life.

383
00:22:07,440 --> 00:22:08,960
I've barked at the plane for too long.

384
00:22:09,840 --> 00:22:12,200
Today, they let this dog on the plane.

385
00:22:13,840 --> 00:22:15,960
Will you take this dog flying with you?

386
00:22:18,960 --> 00:22:21,040
Well, if this dog is going to be this romantic,

387
00:22:22,200 --> 00:22:23,560
I'll take him around the world.

388
00:22:26,680 --> 00:22:27,680
No.

389
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:29,240
Do it again. Say it properly.

390
00:22:29,360 --> 00:22:30,600
You're not a dog anymore.

391
00:22:31,240 --> 00:22:32,800
We're equal now.

392
00:22:33,360 --> 00:22:35,800
Neither is on the ground or in the sky.

393
00:22:37,120 --> 00:22:38,120
Get up.

394
00:22:40,200 --> 00:22:41,920
Then I'll keep it simple, Sek Loso style.

395
00:22:42,640 --> 00:22:47,360
Nit, I love you so f*cking much.

396
00:22:52,640 --> 00:22:53,640
Will you marry me?

397
00:22:58,600 --> 00:23:00,000
Of course, it's a yes.

398
00:23:02,240 --> 00:23:03,240
I freaking will.

399
00:23:16,160 --> 00:23:17,240
Kiss!

400
00:23:17,280 --> 00:23:18,280
Kiss!

401
00:23:18,320 --> 00:23:19,160
Kiss!

402
00:23:19,200 --> 00:23:20,240
That's enough. Thank you.

403
00:23:20,280 --> 00:23:21,040
Kiss!
Kiss!

404
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:22,800
Kiss!
Kiss!

405
00:23:23,760 --> 00:23:24,560
Kiss!
Kiss!

406
00:23:25,440 --> 00:23:26,160
Kiss!
Kiss!

407
00:23:27,040 --> 00:23:28,040
Kiss!

408
00:23:28,120 --> 00:23:29,160
That's enough.

409
00:23:31,240 --> 00:23:34,040
♪ Fly with me, free my heart ♪

410
00:23:34,040 --> 00:23:38,120
♪ Don't be shy, just open your heart ♪

411
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:41,680
♪ Wanna come aboard, give it a try ♪

412
00:23:41,880 --> 00:23:44,440
♪ Love is gonna take off now ♪

413
00:23:46,680 --> 00:23:52,440
♪ Our love is gonna take off now ♪

414
00:24:03,120 --> 00:24:04,120
You should go.

415
00:24:05,080 --> 00:24:06,200
So I can go in there.

416
00:24:06,680 --> 00:24:07,800
You walk in first.

417
00:24:08,840 --> 00:24:11,200
I'll see you off until the last second.

418
00:24:13,880 --> 00:24:15,480
How can I not be sad when you say that?

419
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:18,640
Who knows
when we'll see each other again?

420
00:24:19,720 --> 00:24:20,720
Or when we'll hug

421
00:24:21,200 --> 00:24:22,320
or kiss again.

422
00:24:23,960 --> 00:24:24,800
Hey.

423
00:24:24,920 --> 00:24:27,200
A soldier can come out
and visit their partner.

424
00:24:27,640 --> 00:24:28,960
Aren't you going to visit me?

425
00:24:29,600 --> 00:24:31,640
I don't know
what I'm going to face in the military.

426
00:24:33,480 --> 00:24:35,000
You'll face nothing.

427
00:24:35,080 --> 00:24:37,960
When you get out,
you'll look even more handsome.

428
00:24:38,920 --> 00:24:40,160
But if you find—

429
00:24:40,240 --> 00:24:41,640
I won't.

430
00:24:42,600 --> 00:24:44,000
I'll wait for you.

431
00:24:44,880 --> 00:24:46,320
I'll wait to kiss you again.

432
00:24:47,600 --> 00:24:48,600
Okay.

433
00:24:48,840 --> 00:24:49,840
I believe you now.

434
00:24:50,240 --> 00:24:54,040
If a soldier hits on me,
I'll tell him my boyfriend is waiting.

435
00:24:54,960 --> 00:24:57,880
Every time I do push-ups,
I'll think of your face.

436
00:24:58,960 --> 00:25:00,360
Every time I practice my aim,

437
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:02,440
you'll be my goal.

438
00:25:03,280 --> 00:25:04,520
Are you going to shoot me?

439
00:25:05,720 --> 00:25:06,720
Mm.

440
00:25:07,200 --> 00:25:08,200
Shoot you with a kiss.

441
00:25:20,480 --> 00:25:21,480
Go now,

442
00:25:22,440 --> 00:25:23,600
so I can go inside.

443
00:25:25,640 --> 00:25:27,840
If you don't go, I will.

444
00:25:35,280 --> 00:25:36,400
I'll be waiting.

445
00:25:41,000 --> 00:25:42,040
Smile for me.

446
00:25:43,080 --> 00:25:45,000
I'll remember your face when I miss you.

447
00:25:50,080 --> 00:25:51,080
I'm off.

448
00:26:17,800 --> 00:26:18,960
Oh, shit!

449
00:26:19,440 --> 00:26:20,440
Dad!

450
00:26:23,880 --> 00:26:24,880
Hi, Dad.

451
00:26:25,920 --> 00:26:26,920
Whose dad?

452
00:26:27,320 --> 00:26:28,360
Who's your dad?

453
00:26:30,480 --> 00:26:31,480
Dad.

454
00:26:31,720 --> 00:26:33,320
Why won't you give him a proper welcome?

455
00:26:33,520 --> 00:26:35,080
I don't want to welcome a liar.

456
00:26:37,520 --> 00:26:40,240
Can you at least welcome the guy
who saved your life?

457
00:26:44,000 --> 00:26:45,200
Why are you here?

458
00:26:49,360 --> 00:26:51,080
I have a project to pitch.

459
00:26:52,600 --> 00:26:53,640
What project?

460
00:26:59,720 --> 00:27:01,560
I've come to ask for Kanit's hand in marriage.

461
00:27:02,480 --> 00:27:03,720
You've got some nerve.

462
00:27:05,520 --> 00:27:07,896
What makes you think you're good enough
to come into my home and ask for my son?

463
00:27:07,920 --> 00:27:09,640
Dad, um…

464
00:27:09,640 --> 00:27:10,640
Don't speak.

465
00:27:11,320 --> 00:27:12,400
I'm asking him.

466
00:27:12,920 --> 00:27:13,960
He has to answer.

467
00:27:15,600 --> 00:27:17,600
All my answers are right here.

468
00:27:19,080 --> 00:27:20,080
Beer.

469
00:27:22,320 --> 00:27:23,800
SAVINGS ACCOUNT
Currently,

470
00:27:24,920 --> 00:27:26,600
this is how much I've saved in my account.

471
00:27:27,920 --> 00:27:29,240
EVERYTHING TOTO
ALL-IN-ONE EMERGENCY ASSISTANCE

472
00:27:29,240 --> 00:27:31,720
And this is the 20-year strategic plan

473
00:27:31,760 --> 00:27:32,920
for Kanit and me.

474
00:27:33,320 --> 00:27:36,080
We're investing in a company called.

475
00:27:36,160 --> 00:27:37,440
Everything Toto.

476
00:27:37,960 --> 00:27:41,400
Dad, Mom, you're probably wondering
what this company is all about.

477
00:27:42,640 --> 00:27:44,160
Allow me to explain.

478
00:27:44,560 --> 00:27:46,760
This company provides all kinds of services.

479
00:27:46,880 --> 00:27:48,400
From emergency assistance,

480
00:27:48,560 --> 00:27:49,880
car washes, auto repairs,

481
00:27:49,960 --> 00:27:51,560
tree trimming, to pet care

482
00:27:51,600 --> 00:27:52,480
and delivery services.

483
00:27:52,480 --> 00:27:54,240
We solve whatever problems
people are facing.

484
00:27:54,640 --> 00:27:56,720
Our 5-year plan is to expand our team.

485
00:27:56,800 --> 00:27:58,080
Our 10-year plan

486
00:27:58,160 --> 00:27:59,600
is to open new branches.

487
00:28:00,120 --> 00:28:01,840
And our 20-year plan

488
00:28:02,040 --> 00:28:04,360
is to give Kanit a stable life

489
00:28:04,720 --> 00:28:07,520
and make him the richest man
in the lower south,

490
00:28:07,600 --> 00:28:09,000
right around the Andaman Basin.

491
00:28:09,880 --> 00:28:13,200
All-in-one. Done by Everything Toto.

492
00:28:18,640 --> 00:28:20,160
Wow!

493
00:28:20,560 --> 00:28:21,600
That's really amazing.

494
00:28:24,040 --> 00:28:26,040
That's the end of my proposal presentation.

495
00:28:26,960 --> 00:28:28,040
I like it.

496
00:28:28,480 --> 00:28:29,800
I approve.

497
00:28:34,280 --> 00:28:35,760
But I still don't like it.

498
00:28:38,280 --> 00:28:39,320
Why not, Dad?

499
00:28:39,480 --> 00:28:41,400
He just said he can take care of me.

500
00:28:41,720 --> 00:28:44,720
The important thing I want to hear about
isn't money.

501
00:28:46,160 --> 00:28:47,440
What I want to know is

502
00:28:48,520 --> 00:28:50,600
why it has to be my son Kanit.

503
00:28:56,080 --> 00:28:57,080
Because …

504
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:01,120
it's my heart's command.

505
00:29:05,920 --> 00:29:07,480
Come on, Toto!

506
00:29:07,680 --> 00:29:09,360
This is not the time to quote P'Sek.

507
00:29:09,680 --> 00:29:11,360
Give a serious answer.

508
00:29:11,640 --> 00:29:13,080
I am being serious.

509
00:29:13,760 --> 00:29:16,160
My feelings are following
my heart's command.

510
00:29:16,320 --> 00:29:19,520
I've liked Kanit since the day I got out of
the car and called him Boiling Tofu.

511
00:29:20,360 --> 00:29:22,240
Who else could keep up with
my sharp tongue like he does?

512
00:29:22,240 --> 00:29:23,240
And look at him.

513
00:29:23,280 --> 00:29:24,640
His face. His skin.

514
00:29:25,640 --> 00:29:27,080
He checks every single box for me.

515
00:29:27,880 --> 00:29:29,656
How can anyone say
that's not my heart's command?

516
00:29:29,680 --> 00:29:31,040
Hey.

517
00:29:32,200 --> 00:29:34,680
Answer me, not your friend.

518
00:29:35,360 --> 00:29:36,360
Sorry, Dad.

519
00:29:37,880 --> 00:29:39,000
But it's true.

520
00:29:39,280 --> 00:29:40,640
Ever since I met Kanit,

521
00:29:41,400 --> 00:29:42,600
I started taking vitamins.

522
00:29:43,560 --> 00:29:45,320
Are you kidding?

523
00:29:46,160 --> 00:29:47,920
Are you serious right now?

524
00:29:48,000 --> 00:29:49,480
Of course, I'm serious.

525
00:29:49,800 --> 00:29:51,160
Ever since I met Kanit,

526
00:29:51,640 --> 00:29:52,840
I started taking vitamins

527
00:29:53,880 --> 00:29:55,840
because I want to take good care
of my health

528
00:29:56,360 --> 00:29:58,280
so I can keep taking care of him
for a long time.

529
00:30:00,080 --> 00:30:01,800
He takes care of me so well.

530
00:30:03,080 --> 00:30:04,600
I'm never letting him go.

531
00:30:12,560 --> 00:30:14,000
I already love it.

532
00:30:14,800 --> 00:30:15,880
What should we do, hon?

533
00:30:16,240 --> 00:30:18,680
Well, I love it.

534
00:30:25,960 --> 00:30:27,120
I'm sold.

535
00:30:31,920 --> 00:30:33,480
I'm buying your sincerity.

536
00:30:34,120 --> 00:30:38,600
You've made me see
that my son has a place in your future.

537
00:30:39,080 --> 00:30:40,360
You're for real. You pass.

538
00:30:41,120 --> 00:30:43,920
You have my permission
to be my future son-in-law

539
00:30:43,920 --> 00:30:46,000
from this moment on.

540
00:30:48,640 --> 00:30:49,640
You did it.

541
00:30:51,760 --> 00:30:53,400
But don't you ever break my son's heart,

542
00:30:54,280 --> 00:30:55,960
or you'll take a bullet.

543
00:30:57,040 --> 00:30:58,200
Don't worry, Dad.

544
00:30:58,800 --> 00:31:00,800
With me, he'll never shed a tear.

545
00:31:14,280 --> 00:31:16,400
Hooo...

546
00:31:16,440 --> 00:31:19,640
Ho-ho-ho-ho…

547
00:31:19,720 --> 00:31:21,880
Hiew!

548
00:31:21,920 --> 00:31:23,560
Ho…

549
00:31:23,560 --> 00:31:26,600
He-o-he-o-he-o-he-o…

550
00:31:26,840 --> 00:31:28,440
Hiew!

551
00:31:28,520 --> 00:31:29,360
Hooo...

552
00:31:29,400 --> 00:31:31,880
Ho-ho-ho-ho…

553
00:31:31,920 --> 00:31:34,160
Hiew!

554
00:31:48,760 --> 00:31:49,320
Hello.
Hello, everyone.

555
00:31:49,920 --> 00:31:50,920
Hello.

556
00:31:51,840 --> 00:31:54,120
Can I pass through?

557
00:31:54,440 --> 00:31:55,920
Hold on.

558
00:31:55,960 --> 00:31:59,520
Before you pass,
you have to give us the Southern password.

559
00:32:00,120 --> 00:32:02,240
Oh, there's something Kanit always says.

560
00:32:03,320 --> 00:32:04,120
“Motherf*cker.”
“F*cking hell.”

561
00:32:05,400 --> 00:32:06,320
“D*ckhead.”
This is an auspicious occasion.

562
00:32:07,320 --> 00:32:08,640
It's not those words.

563
00:32:08,760 --> 00:32:09,640
Oh, no?

564
00:32:09,720 --> 00:32:10,720
No.

565
00:32:11,760 --> 00:32:13,160
But Kanit always says those things.

566
00:32:15,360 --> 00:32:16,480
Oh, I know what it is.

567
00:32:18,240 --> 00:32:20,360
“I'm not someone who talks nonsense.
I always speak the truth. I don't lie.

568
00:32:20,360 --> 00:32:22,160
“I'm devoted to one love. If you don't believe me,
go see a tiger riding a monkey.

569
00:32:22,160 --> 00:32:24,200
“If it's not true,
go see a monkey riding a tiger!”

570
00:32:26,000 --> 00:32:27,000
There it is.

571
00:32:28,040 --> 00:32:29,080
Pass on through.

572
00:32:29,120 --> 00:32:30,120
Thank you.

573
00:32:36,960 --> 00:32:37,680
Pailin.

574
00:32:37,720 --> 00:32:38,960
Please go easy on me.

575
00:32:40,280 --> 00:32:41,400
Mr. Toto.

576
00:32:42,280 --> 00:32:43,800
You want to marry a flight attendant.

577
00:32:43,960 --> 00:32:50,080
I want to know if you even know
how to make an in-flight announcement.

578
00:32:52,720 --> 00:32:54,880
That's not beyond me.

579
00:32:54,920 --> 00:32:56,400
Yeah!

580
00:32:56,480 --> 00:32:58,440
Let's hear it.

581
00:32:59,280 --> 00:33:02,640
This is the final call
for Everything Toto Airlines.

582
00:33:03,560 --> 00:33:06,280
Flight TT 216,

583
00:33:07,840 --> 00:33:10,880
now boarding for Kanit's heart.

584
00:33:12,840 --> 00:33:16,920
All passengers,
please proceed to Toto's heart.

585
00:33:20,480 --> 00:33:21,520
How did I do?

586
00:33:21,760 --> 00:33:22,760
Did I pass?

587
00:33:23,080 --> 00:33:23,760
You passed!

588
00:33:23,800 --> 00:33:25,520
You're cleared for takeoff.

589
00:33:28,160 --> 00:33:29,160
Thank you.

590
00:33:30,880 --> 00:33:32,120
This way.

591
00:33:38,920 --> 00:33:40,120
Hello, Dad and Mom.

592
00:33:40,720 --> 00:33:42,480
Hello.

593
00:33:43,480 --> 00:33:45,800
Are you ready to accept a rescue worker
as your son-in-law?

594
00:33:46,600 --> 00:33:47,600
Ready, hon?

595
00:33:48,360 --> 00:33:50,000
I've been ready for a long time.

596
00:33:51,440 --> 00:33:53,480
My son-in-law is so handsome.

597
00:33:55,960 --> 00:33:56,960
Amazing.

598
00:34:03,400 --> 00:34:10,640
WEDDING CEREMONY
KANIT & PANUPONG 12 DECEMBER 2026

599
00:34:13,200 --> 00:34:14,600
Do you like the dress I bought you?

600
00:34:15,520 --> 00:34:16,600
Is it to your liking?

601
00:34:17,480 --> 00:34:18,480
It's pretty, Mom.

602
00:34:18,600 --> 00:34:20,320
I'm so glad to be here today.

603
00:34:22,360 --> 00:34:23,640
To see your brother happy.

604
00:34:26,000 --> 00:34:28,160
Just this chance from him

605
00:34:29,680 --> 00:34:34,040
takes a huge weight of guilt off my chest,

606
00:34:34,800 --> 00:34:37,080
even though he doesn't let me
be a part of his life.

607
00:34:43,480 --> 00:34:45,320
He might change his mind one day.

608
00:34:56,760 --> 00:34:58,016
Come on. Let's take some photos together.

609
00:34:58,040 --> 00:34:59,040
Okay.

610
00:35:00,920 --> 00:35:02,360
Let's see.

611
00:35:03,920 --> 00:35:05,560
One. Two. Three.

612
00:35:10,880 --> 00:35:12,800
Cheers!

613
00:35:13,320 --> 00:35:14,040
Hey.

614
00:35:14,280 --> 00:35:15,280
Honestly,

615
00:35:15,520 --> 00:35:16,720
I can't believe

616
00:35:16,920 --> 00:35:18,200
rescue workers like us

617
00:35:18,720 --> 00:35:20,520
get to hang out with people in this league.

618
00:35:20,840 --> 00:35:21,520
Yeah.

619
00:35:21,560 --> 00:35:22,680
You know what?

620
00:35:22,800 --> 00:35:24,336
I might go for a walk around the airport.

621
00:35:24,360 --> 00:35:27,400
Maybe I'll run into a handsome captain
or flight attendant.

622
00:35:29,200 --> 00:35:30,760
Oh, Pailin.

623
00:35:31,000 --> 00:35:32,920
Do you have any handsome guys
to introduce me to?

624
00:35:37,000 --> 00:35:38,040
I know a few.

625
00:35:38,120 --> 00:35:39,680
See?

626
00:35:40,360 --> 00:35:42,960
- Here we go.
- But a captain?

627
00:35:43,320 --> 00:35:46,000
If I find one, I'm keeping him for myself.

628
00:35:47,600 --> 00:35:48,600
Queen move.

629
00:35:49,040 --> 00:35:49,720
As she should.

630
00:35:49,760 --> 00:35:51,400
There goes my chance of getting my wings.

631
00:35:51,560 --> 00:35:52,560
This girl stole it.

632
00:35:52,920 --> 00:35:55,520
But before we get to your happy ending,

633
00:35:55,800 --> 00:35:57,776
we should keep our fingers crossed
for Ki and Veha.

634
00:35:57,800 --> 00:35:59,360
Yeah.

635
00:36:00,240 --> 00:36:01,280
I don't know.

636
00:36:03,240 --> 00:36:05,736
When it comes to this, I shouldn't be
the only one talking about it, right?

637
00:36:05,760 --> 00:36:06,880
He needs to say it, too.

638
00:36:08,800 --> 00:36:10,000
It's not like I don't want to,

639
00:36:11,160 --> 00:36:12,480
but he hasn't asked yet.

640
00:36:15,120 --> 00:36:17,256
I have to wait for him to finish
his military service first.

641
00:36:17,280 --> 00:36:18,640
- Got it.
- Got it.

642
00:36:18,880 --> 00:36:19,920
Come on. Cheers.

643
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:20,560
Cheers?

644
00:36:20,560 --> 00:36:22,440
Let's drink to drown our worries!

645
00:36:22,480 --> 00:36:23,800
Yeah!

646
00:36:23,800 --> 00:36:24,360
Woo!

647
00:36:24,360 --> 00:36:25,480
Bottoms up.

648
00:36:25,520 --> 00:36:26,520
Seriously?

649
00:36:29,560 --> 00:36:30,560
If I asked,

650
00:36:30,640 --> 00:36:31,760
would you say yes?

651
00:36:32,280 --> 00:36:32,920
Hey.

652
00:36:32,960 --> 00:36:34,160
Ki!

653
00:36:36,120 --> 00:36:37,400
I thought you weren't coming.

654
00:36:37,760 --> 00:36:38,960
It's my dear brother's wedding.

655
00:36:38,960 --> 00:36:40,000
How could I miss it?

656
00:36:41,680 --> 00:36:42,360
Sit down, bro.

657
00:36:42,400 --> 00:36:43,696
You should've told us you were coming.

658
00:36:43,720 --> 00:36:44,720
Come on.

659
00:36:45,560 --> 00:36:46,560
Besides,

660
00:36:48,440 --> 00:36:50,200
I missed my boyfriend so bad.

661
00:36:50,280 --> 00:36:52,680
Oh!

662
00:36:53,000 --> 00:36:54,520
Stop it.

663
00:36:55,280 --> 00:36:56,896
If you missed me,
why didn't you call me more often?

664
00:36:56,920 --> 00:36:58,240
Yeah.

665
00:36:59,280 --> 00:37:00,576
My training has been super intense.

666
00:37:00,600 --> 00:37:01,640
They took my phone.

667
00:37:02,400 --> 00:37:03,920
I've tried my best.

668
00:37:04,400 --> 00:37:05,440
Please don't be mad at me.

669
00:37:05,640 --> 00:37:06,640
Please don't sulk.

670
00:37:09,440 --> 00:37:11,000
We don't get to see each other often.

671
00:37:11,240 --> 00:37:12,280
I won't sulk.

672
00:37:12,800 --> 00:37:15,136
I'd rather spend our time loving each other
and making everyone here jealous.

673
00:37:15,160 --> 00:37:16,960
Sure.

674
00:37:17,000 --> 00:37:18,656
- He was looking this way.
- I'm so jealous.

675
00:37:18,680 --> 00:37:21,320
Por, I want that!

676
00:37:22,400 --> 00:37:23,680
Wait until you're a big girl.

677
00:37:25,800 --> 00:37:26,600
Stop it.

678
00:37:26,680 --> 00:37:28,280
I know I'm only 156 cm tall.

679
00:37:29,000 --> 00:37:30,000
Enough.

680
00:37:30,360 --> 00:37:32,120
Let's make them even more jealous.

681
00:37:35,920 --> 00:37:36,640
Bro!

682
00:37:36,640 --> 00:37:39,280
You guys are stealing the spotlight
from the hosts!

683
00:37:40,320 --> 00:37:42,880
Our wedding can't be any less grand
than To's.

684
00:37:44,560 --> 00:37:45,800
I wouldn't let anyone outdo me.

685
00:37:46,040 --> 00:37:47,560
Oh!

686
00:37:48,200 --> 00:37:49,040
I can't wait to see it.

687
00:37:49,080 --> 00:37:50,360
Hello. One. Two. Three.

688
00:37:51,360 --> 00:37:53,240
And now,

689
00:37:53,640 --> 00:37:56,400
I'd like to invite Village Head Kwaed

690
00:37:56,760 --> 00:37:59,400
to come up
and offer a blessing to the newlyweds.

691
00:38:00,760 --> 00:38:01,760
Thank you.

692
00:38:07,240 --> 00:38:09,040
The groom and I

693
00:38:09,360 --> 00:38:10,880
have known each other for a long time.

694
00:38:11,280 --> 00:38:14,320
His name is… Kanit.

695
00:38:15,600 --> 00:38:16,880
We're neighbors.

696
00:38:17,520 --> 00:38:19,200
I've seen him since he was a kid.

697
00:38:20,200 --> 00:38:22,880
And today, he's finally settling down
and starting his own family.

698
00:38:23,040 --> 00:38:25,560
Being life partners is a journey.

699
00:38:26,800 --> 00:38:27,960
Hold hands tightly

700
00:38:28,800 --> 00:38:30,760
through thick and thin.

701
00:38:32,640 --> 00:38:35,840
I wish for you to be life partners

702
00:38:36,200 --> 00:38:38,120
who are best friends—

703
00:38:38,360 --> 00:38:39,720
knowing each other's hearts,

704
00:38:40,280 --> 00:38:41,760
and understanding each other forever.

705
00:38:43,280 --> 00:38:44,280
Thank you.

706
00:38:47,160 --> 00:38:48,400
You know the village head?

707
00:38:49,520 --> 00:38:50,960
I've never met him before.

708
00:38:52,680 --> 00:38:54,560
Thank you so much, sir,

709
00:38:54,800 --> 00:38:58,880
for honoring us
by wishing the newlyweds well.

710
00:38:59,000 --> 00:39:00,040
Thank you so much.

711
00:39:00,080 --> 00:39:00,960
Thank you.

712
00:39:01,040 --> 00:39:02,760
Thank you.

713
00:39:08,880 --> 00:39:09,880
Next,

714
00:39:10,040 --> 00:39:11,680
I'd like to invite the newlyweds

715
00:39:11,880 --> 00:39:16,040
to say a few words to our guests.

716
00:39:19,120 --> 00:39:20,120
To!

717
00:39:27,640 --> 00:39:28,640
(Shut up!)

718
00:39:31,760 --> 00:39:32,600
Alright.

719
00:39:32,680 --> 00:39:36,200
Thank you to all our honored guests
for coming to our wedding.

720
00:39:36,920 --> 00:39:39,400
I don't have much to say,

721
00:39:40,000 --> 00:39:42,680
except that from now on,

722
00:39:43,080 --> 00:39:45,400
no matter what comes our way,

723
00:39:45,840 --> 00:39:51,040
I promise we'll face
and get through it all together.

724
00:39:58,960 --> 00:40:00,320
Come on. Say something.

725
00:40:01,440 --> 00:40:02,320
I don't like public speaking.
Just say anything.

726
00:40:03,000 --> 00:40:04,000
Woo!

727
00:40:06,240 --> 00:40:07,240
Alright.

728
00:40:07,680 --> 00:40:08,680
I…

729
00:40:09,360 --> 00:40:10,520
I'm not good with words.

730
00:40:10,920 --> 00:40:13,760
But I actually have something to say
to everyone.

731
00:40:15,840 --> 00:40:16,840
I think

732
00:40:17,600 --> 00:40:19,560
the electricity bill has been
so expensive lately.

733
00:40:20,840 --> 00:40:23,440
And you guys are using a lot of power.

734
00:40:24,000 --> 00:40:25,000
Look.

735
00:40:25,560 --> 00:40:26,800
You turned on so many lights.

736
00:40:27,080 --> 00:40:28,120
It's so bright out here.

737
00:40:28,880 --> 00:40:33,480
But there's this one light
that shines the brightest in my heart.

738
00:40:36,200 --> 00:40:37,200
This one.

739
00:40:53,040 --> 00:40:54,920
Hell no, I'm not letting you get married!

740
00:40:54,960 --> 00:40:55,680
Definitely not!

741
00:40:55,720 --> 00:40:56,720
That's right!

742
00:40:58,240 --> 00:40:59,280
What's going on?

743
00:40:59,560 --> 00:41:00,560
Is he your ex?

744
00:41:01,120 --> 00:41:02,200
No.

745
00:41:02,520 --> 00:41:04,040
- I don't even know who he is.
- Oh?

746
00:41:04,080 --> 00:41:05,856
Once you get married,
you're just gonna end up divorced anyway!

747
00:41:05,880 --> 00:41:07,920
Love isn't real!

748
00:41:08,160 --> 00:41:09,680
Love makes you blind!

749
00:41:09,760 --> 00:41:10,560
Yeah!

750
00:41:10,640 --> 00:41:12,200
That you can't see the truth!

751
00:41:12,720 --> 00:41:13,840
He's quoting Toon Bodyslam.

752
00:41:14,160 --> 00:41:15,200
What's going on?

753
00:41:16,000 --> 00:41:18,320
Weddings are nonsense!

754
00:41:22,760 --> 00:41:24,000
How is he that drunk?

755
00:41:24,000 --> 00:41:25,280
Hey!

756
00:41:25,560 --> 00:41:26,360
He's having a seizure!

757
00:41:26,360 --> 00:41:28,360
Why are these people lying on the ground?

758
00:41:29,400 --> 00:41:30,400
What's going on?

759
00:41:30,720 --> 00:41:31,320
How are they?

760
00:41:31,360 --> 00:41:32,600
Could it be the bootleg liquor?

761
00:41:32,880 --> 00:41:33,880
Bootleg liquor?

762
00:41:35,000 --> 00:41:36,400
He's drooling.

763
00:41:37,400 --> 00:41:39,360
- What should we do?
- I'm going to check on them.

764
00:41:39,880 --> 00:41:40,880
I'll help.

765
00:41:41,360 --> 00:41:42,360
To.

766
00:41:42,480 --> 00:41:44,480
Tong, Beer, Ki, check on them.

767
00:41:44,960 --> 00:41:46,200
Give them first aid.

768
00:41:46,280 --> 00:41:46,920
Okay.
Sure.

769
00:41:47,520 --> 00:41:48,520
Let's go.

770
00:41:48,560 --> 00:41:51,160
Ja-O, radio for backup at the scene immediately.

771
00:41:51,680 --> 00:41:52,816
And get a sample of that liquor.

772
00:41:52,840 --> 00:41:53,840
Okay.

773
00:41:54,360 --> 00:41:55,480
He's already drooling.

774
00:41:56,120 --> 00:41:58,280
He's already drooling.

775
00:41:58,320 --> 00:41:58,880
Hey.

776
00:41:58,880 --> 00:41:59,976
Can I get a cloth to rest his head on?

777
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:01,000
- Sure.
- Bring it now.

778
00:42:01,720 --> 00:42:02,776
Everyone, please stay back.

779
00:42:02,800 --> 00:42:03,640
Give us some space.

780
00:42:03,760 --> 00:42:04,960
Let us clear the area.

781
00:42:05,240 --> 00:42:06,360
Please don't crowd around.

782
00:42:07,640 --> 00:42:08,640
Look!

783
00:42:08,720 --> 00:42:09,600
Excuse me.

784
00:42:09,720 --> 00:42:10,720
Here you go.

785
00:42:33,240 --> 00:42:34,440
I appreciate your help, Ki.

786
00:42:34,600 --> 00:42:36,976
You came straight from the military
and didn't even get a chance to rest.

787
00:42:37,000 --> 00:42:37,760
Damn.
It's okay.

788
00:42:38,760 --> 00:42:41,760
I could really use some excitement
in my life right now.

789
00:42:43,720 --> 00:42:45,680
Thanks a lot for coming all the way
to my wedding.

790
00:42:46,320 --> 00:42:47,680
Congratulations.

791
00:42:48,080 --> 00:42:50,840
But honestly, your wedding
isn't as important

792
00:42:51,560 --> 00:42:53,040
as seeing my boyfriend.

793
00:42:54,760 --> 00:42:55,800
Yeah, I know.

794
00:42:56,280 --> 00:42:57,360
I'm heading out now.

795
00:42:57,920 --> 00:42:59,680
I've been deprived for too long.

796
00:42:59,840 --> 00:43:01,000
Time to get some action.

797
00:43:03,240 --> 00:43:03,960
You're so annoying.
Hurry up and get going.

798
00:43:04,800 --> 00:43:05,800
Congratulations.

799
00:43:06,240 --> 00:43:06,880
Thanks.

800
00:43:06,880 --> 00:43:08,080
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

801
00:43:13,680 --> 00:43:16,600
It was supposed to be an auspicious day,
but we had to deal with all that.

802
00:43:17,480 --> 00:43:19,080
I'm a rescue worker.

803
00:43:19,400 --> 00:43:21,320
That's a 24/7 job.

804
00:43:23,200 --> 00:43:24,200
See?

805
00:43:24,360 --> 00:43:26,040
Being with me takes toughness.

806
00:43:26,400 --> 00:43:28,160
You risk both body and heart.

807
00:43:31,000 --> 00:43:32,040
Yeah, I know.

808
00:43:32,040 --> 00:43:34,720
If I weren't willing to take that risk,
I wouldn't have married you.

809
00:43:37,680 --> 00:43:39,640
Well, the wedding turned into
a complete disaster.

810
00:43:40,000 --> 00:43:42,080
That was such a life-and-death moment.

811
00:43:45,160 --> 00:43:46,800
You and I will never live in peace.

812
00:43:46,920 --> 00:43:49,080
There'll always be chaos
to keep us entertained.

813
00:43:53,240 --> 00:43:57,320
Let's keep loving, bickering,
and fighting like this forever.

814
00:43:58,280 --> 00:44:00,520
Can we just love each other?

815
00:44:00,800 --> 00:44:02,160
No more fighting. It's exhausting.

816
00:44:03,480 --> 00:44:04,920
How about fighting in bed instead?

817
00:44:06,440 --> 00:44:10,000
Your mind is always in the gutter.

818
00:44:10,720 --> 00:44:12,960
Say something romantic for once.

819
00:44:14,040 --> 00:44:15,440
I don't know how to be romantic.

820
00:44:15,760 --> 00:44:17,160
I only know how to be blunt.

821
00:44:17,760 --> 00:44:18,920
Alright, just be blunt then.

822
00:44:20,480 --> 00:44:21,920
As long as I get to marry you,

823
00:44:22,680 --> 00:44:24,256
it doesn't matter
if I have enough to get by or not.

824
00:44:24,280 --> 00:44:25,800
It doesn't matter if I'm dirt poor.

825
00:44:26,200 --> 00:44:27,440
I can sleep anywhere,

826
00:44:28,360 --> 00:44:29,560
as long as I get to sleep

827
00:44:31,520 --> 00:44:32,520
next to you.

828
00:44:32,840 --> 00:44:33,840
Oh.

829
00:44:34,320 --> 00:44:35,440
You're copying P'Sek again.

830
00:44:35,560 --> 00:44:39,000
Come on. He's my idol
when it comes to romance.

831
00:44:46,480 --> 00:44:47,720
Will you accept my love,

832
00:44:48,880 --> 00:44:50,240
Mr. Boiling Tofu?

833
00:44:54,160 --> 00:44:55,200
Of course, I will.

834
00:44:55,920 --> 00:44:57,560
Mr. Black-Smoke Barking Dog.

835
00:45:02,800 --> 00:45:05,840
♪ With you and me together ♪

836
00:45:05,880 --> 00:45:08,640
♪ Every day, just like this ♪

837
00:45:08,680 --> 00:45:11,320
♪ Through both the good and stormy weather ♪

838
00:45:11,400 --> 00:45:14,680
♪ Love needs no reason for this ♪

839
00:45:14,800 --> 00:45:16,560
♪ It can't be wrong ♪

840
00:45:16,920 --> 00:45:19,520
♪ To not care what people say ♪

841
00:45:19,640 --> 00:45:22,360
♪ When it comes to me and you ♪

842
00:45:22,440 --> 00:45:25,080
♪ We are the reason that stays ♪

843
00:45:27,600 --> 00:45:28,760
Let's take this inside.

844
00:45:58,800 --> 00:46:00,000
Dear passenger.

845
00:46:00,320 --> 00:46:02,760
Welcome to tonight's flight.

846
00:46:03,280 --> 00:46:04,960
Please check your seat.

847
00:46:05,440 --> 00:46:08,200
Exits are located at the front
and back of the cabin.

848
00:46:08,880 --> 00:46:12,160
In case of emergency, please remain calm

849
00:46:12,680 --> 00:46:15,200
and follow the cabin crew's instructions.

850
00:46:15,920 --> 00:46:17,520
It's my first time flying first class.

851
00:46:18,160 --> 00:46:19,280
I don't understand anything.

852
00:46:20,360 --> 00:46:21,800
In that case,

853
00:46:22,280 --> 00:46:23,400
please start by

854
00:46:24,640 --> 00:46:26,080
unbuttoning your shirt.

855
00:46:32,080 --> 00:46:33,080
What's next?

856
00:46:34,640 --> 00:46:38,040
Now, what would you like?

857
00:46:41,160 --> 00:46:42,160
Coffee?

858
00:46:43,240 --> 00:46:44,240
Or tea?

859
00:46:46,960 --> 00:46:49,280
Or me?

860
00:46:51,840 --> 00:46:53,280
What should I get?

861
00:46:57,640 --> 00:46:58,640
I can't hold it anymore.

862
00:46:58,920 --> 00:47:00,280
Can we start now?

863
00:47:01,240 --> 00:47:05,200
Sir, please.
No sexual harassment of the cabin crew.

864
00:47:05,920 --> 00:47:07,120
I'm not your passenger.

865
00:47:08,360 --> 00:47:09,480
I'm your husband.

866
00:47:25,680 --> 00:47:26,280
Stop staring.

867
00:47:26,320 --> 00:47:27,320
We're about to bang.
